messages:
tess_cs: ACME Corp onboarding stuck. They see 401s on first auth, then a sudden flood of 429s. They mentioned an edge gateway + envoy sidecar.
tess_cs: ACME infra note: "gateway appends analytics cookie (~420b) and we use Bearer token; sometimes auth fails."
omar_eng: Likely header size overflow or header truncation. If Authorization gets mangled the handshake returns 401.
vikram_sre: When clients immediately retry without jitter we see many short connections and preflight spikes -> 429 from our rate limiter.
megan_support: They're on node-sdk v0.9.2. Can we give a quick workaround?
omar_eng: Fast fixes: 1) strip analytics cookie on /v1/auth route at the gateway. 2) move analytics payload to a POST body to a different internal endpoint. 3) add jittered exponential backoff to auth retries in the SDK or as a wrapper.
acme_infra: We can add a route rule to exclude /v1/auth from cookie injection. We'll try that now.
omar_eng: Also suggest upgrading to node-sdk v0.9.6 which has an initial-splay and preflight coalescing toggle. If upgrade blocked, this tiny wrapper helps:
```
async function authWithJitter(fn, attempts=5){
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    try{return await fn();}
    catch(e){await sleep(Math.pow(2,i)*100 + Math.floor(Math.random()*100));}
  }
  throw Error('auth failed');
}
```
vikram_sre: Ops action: add onboarding doc note for "gateway header-size and cookie interactions" and emit metric for Authorization length on first-failure traces.
megan_support: ACME applied route strip; 401s stopped. After applying jitter wrapper retries collapsed and 429s disappeared.
tess_cs: Great outcome. I'll update renewal tracker and add follow-up to ensure SDK upgrade during production rollout. :thumbsup:
